Title: What They Called Recovery
Credit: Animated feature screenplay — scene draft
Author: Christopher Kokkinos
Draft date: 2026-09-28
Status: SC017 proposed for individual author scene review; combined pass provisionally accepted

INT. HELEN AND BRIAN'S HOUSE - MONDAY PRE-DAWN - ZOE'S ACCOUNT

At midnight the spare phone still has no call from Jackie. Zoe tells Helen and Brian the agreed rule: no call means the real route is exposed. Helen says Mac's trip was already arranged. Brian takes the phone and switches it off. They refuse to call police. Zoe looks from the chained front door to Brian at the back door, weighing the noise Jackie told her to make.

In her room Zoe opens the folder for the first time. The childhood photograph and repeated number. ORIGINAL and ASSIGNED IDENTITY fields. Medical notes. A payment record. Mac's legal name as authorising client. Helen and Brian named as receiving placement. She finds no adoption order in this folder. She looks up at real photographs of the life she has lived with them. The folder changes her understanding of its arrangement, not the fact those years happened.

Helen brings clean clothes. Zoe says the trip is unsafe; Helen admits it may be and still prepares her for it. Zoe packs the folder and still-unopened black drive beneath ordinary things. One backpack, no suitcase. At 04:10 a car arrives. Helen embraces her and whispers an apology without naming what she means. Brian opens the door. Zoe goes out because travel may offer an opening she cannot find inside the house.

INT./EXT. CAR/DEPARTURES/AIRCRAFT - MONDAY - ZOE'S ACCOUNT

The unnamed DRIVER takes her to an airport. A navy-coated ESCORT with a folder receives the travel documents. At check-in and security, prefilled answers and a signed consent form pass through ordinary procedure. Zoe watches her bag travel through the scanner and takes it back immediately. No staff member is shown knowing what she carries or why she fears the destination.

The escort hands Zoe Elias's photograph and leaves before the gate. Asked the supposed grandmother's name, she refers Zoe back to Mac's arrangement instead of answering. Zoe boards with the backpack under the seat, one shoe through its strap. She studies Mac's handwriting on the photograph: HE IS HARMLESS. DO EXACTLY WHAT HE SAYS.

The aircraft lifts. Zoe sees no attempt to stop her. She does not know whether anyone has the real route, only that Jackie knew it and failed to call. She decides to run at the first opening after arrival.

INT. ELIAS'S CAR - MOTORWAY - PRESENT DAY

ZOE
Harmless meant controllable. Your photograph helped me identify you. It didn't make me trust you.

ELIAS
He sent me yours and said it would help you trust me.

They both understand how little those photographs established.
